==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{dercat|ang|gem-pro|ine-pro|inh=2}}
From {{inh|ang|gmw-pro|*leudan}}.

{{rel-top|Cognates}}
Cognates include {{cog|osx|liodan}}, {{cog|goh|liotan}}, {{cog|got|𐌻𐌹𐌿𐌳𐌰𐌽}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{desc|fa|رستن|tr=rostan}}, Albanian {{m|sq|lind||to be born, to spring}} < {{m|sq|lej||to generate, produce, give birth to}}, Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ἐλεύθερος||free, freeman}}, Latin {{m|la|liber||free}}, Old Irish {{m|sga|luss||plant}}. {{rel-bottom}}

